  "provenance_notes": {
    "fm_towns_symbols": "First-person June 2025 statement supports presence of debug symbols; symbol completeness and code/data equivalence to this DOS executable have not been verified.",
    "game_version_identity": "The local readme says the bundle came from bestoldgames.net. Local PRINCE.DAT and multiple related data/assets match the TASVideos 290415-byte unknown-v1.0 / Initial Release manifest, but local PRINCE.EXE and PRINCE2.EX_ hashes do not match its PRINCE.EXE MD5. Record the data-set relationship as evidence only; executable release identity remains unclassified.",
    "main_backup_diff": "At root link address 0x052d:0x129d (file byte 34157), PRINCE.EXE writes byte [DS:03e2]=1 then unconditionally jumps to 0x53f4; PRINCE2.EX_ compares word [DS:03e2] with zero and enters initialization at 0x052d:0x12a7 only if zero. The next block writes word [03e2] and calls 0x052d:0x44e7 and 0x052d:0x4569. No version/correctness conclusion is implied.",
    "rtlink_version": "The executable embeds an RTLink(R)/Plus runtime error marker, confirming linker/runtime provenance. It contains no exact version evidence. Contemporary literature establishes RTLink/Plus 4.0 in 1991, a 5.1 catalog listing in 1993, and a 7.10 user-reported banner in 1994; none identifies this build.",
    "reference_code_use": "Use parser, entry seed lists, and metadata as a comparison aid. Do not import generated emulation C as reconstruction."
